<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balangir</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bolangir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balangir, also spelt Bolangir, is a town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and headquarters of Balangir district. It replaced Patnagarh as the capital of the princely state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patna">Patna</a>, which merged with the province of Orissa in 1948. The surrounding district is largely agricultural and known for its hand-woven textiles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balangir.jpg" alt="Balangir" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Satyajit Nayak at English Wikipedia · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balangir_palace.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
